ink of  serb orthodox people  and he's afraid they bring back more  infections as they did  partly in summertime these measures now  should be imposed in a way that nobody  really travels  and everybody stays home if this will  function we will see  later on but i doubt about the  functional ability of this  because not every bear control is so  maximized that you can exclude  infections coming in again into the  country  either from the south or from the north  of course it's always a struggle klaus  plumpers in vienna thank you for those  insights  you're welcome and for more on this i'm  joined by dr claudia hansen an  epidemiologist at the karolinska  institute in  stockholm uh thank you for joining us  doctor sweden  is tightening its restrictions what are  the new measures and  why the big change  good morning from stockholm uh the big  change is that the country is realizing  that the present strategy  does not really protect the the most  vulnerable and the old people  so they realize a bit that the  particularly the promise which was given  in the spring  that there wouldn't be a second wave  because of uh reached herd immunity  doesn't hold  so that is changing the public opinion  which is very important  i'm not sure whether the present  measures will really bring the case  numbers  tremendously down after hearing yeah  the government is now recommending that  passengers wear masks on public  transport but won't make them  mandatory will that work  i don't know they have been telling the  public two months  no two two to six months that must do  not work  i'm not sure how voluntary measure  now can can work in public transport it  it will become very difficult  and and your country as we heard in the  report it went it alone at the beginning  of the outbreak when other european  countries  lock down is can we now say that that  was the wrong approach  i personally think it's the wrong  approach and it's a it's a wrong  discussion to think about  lockdown 